{
  "_id": "galatians1",
  "book": {
    "_id": "galatians",
    "title": "Galatians",
    "titleShort": "Gal.",
    "titleOfficial": "THE EPISTLE OF PAUL THE APOSTLE TO THE",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Galatians",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "Preachers of false gospels are accursed—Paul received the gospel by revelation—He believed, was taught, and preached to the Gentiles.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Paul, an apostle, (not of men, neither by man, but by Jesus Christ, and God the Father, who raised him from the dead;)",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Apostles; Priesthood, Authority."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And all the brethren which are with me, unto the churches of Galatia:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Grace be to you and peace from God the Father, and from our Lord Jesus Christ,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Who gave himself for our sins, that he might deliver us from this present evil world, according to the will of God and our Father:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Redeemer."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Redemption."
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "TG God, Will of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To whom be glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I marvel that ye are so soon removed from him that called you into the grace of Christ unto another gospel:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Apostasy of Individuals; Apostasy of the Early Christian Church."
          },
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "2 Cor. 11:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Which is not another; but there be some that trouble you, and would pervert the gospel of Christ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "GR agitate, raise doubts, perplex."
          },
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 75,
            "text": "Gal. 5:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "TG Gospel."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But though we, or an angel from heaven, preach any other gospel unto you than that which we have preached unto you, let him be accursed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Angels."
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "1 Tim. 1:3."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Gospel."
          },
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 135,
            "text": "Gal. 5:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "As we said before, so say I now again, If any man preach any other gospel unto you than that ye have received, let him be accursed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG False Doctrine."
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 130,
            "text": "2 Ne. 28:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For do I now persuade men, or God? or do I seek to please men? for if I yet pleased men, I should not be the servant of Christ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "GR appease, aspire to the favor of. JST Gal. 1:10 … please …"
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Peer Influence."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 83,
            "text": "TG Courage."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But I certify you, brethren, that the gospel which was preached of me is not after man.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "GR declare, make known to."
          },
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "2 Cor. 4:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For I neither received it of man, neither was I taught it, but by the revelation of Jesus Christ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "GR from a man."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "GR through a revelation."
          },
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "1 Cor. 9:1; D&C 84:1. TG Testimony."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 58
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For ye have heard of my conversation in time past in the Jews’ religion, how that beyond measure I persecuted the church of God, and wasted it:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "GR conduct."
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 109,
            "text": "Acts 9:21 (10–22)."
          },
          {
            "start": 133,
            "end": 139,
            "text": "GR was ravaging, destroying."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And profited in the Jews’ religion above many my equals in mine own nation, being more exceedingly zealous of the traditions of my fathers.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "GR was advancing."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "GR men of my age."
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 106,
            "text": "TG Zeal."
          },
          {
            "start": 114,
            "end": 124,
            "text": "TG Traditions of Men."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But when it pleased God, who separated me from my mother’s womb, and called me by his grace,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "To reveal his Son in me, that I might preach him among the heathen; immediately I conferred not with flesh and blood:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "GR nations, Gentiles. TG Heathen."
          },
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "TG Flesh and Blood."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither went I up to Jerusalem to them which were apostles before me; but I went into Arabia, and returned again unto Damascus.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Then after three years I went up to Jerusalem to see Peter, and abode with him fifteen days.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "Acts 9:26."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But other of the apostles saw I none, save James the Lord’s brother.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "TG Apostles."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Acts 21:18."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Family of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now the things which I write unto you, behold, before God, I lie not.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Scriptures, Writing of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Afterwards I came into the regions of Syria and Cilicia;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And was unknown by face unto the churches of Judæa which were in Christ:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But they had heard only, That he which persecuted us in times past now preacheth the faith which once he destroyed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And they glorified God in me.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "galatians2",
  "prevChapterId": "2corinthians13",
